Initial release — branches, staff and opening hours

What the business is made of, and who works in it.

It also publishes StaffDirectoryContract, which is load-bearing well beyond
this module. Four other modules record `recorded_by` against a cash or ledger
row, and that column means staff_members.id — not the signed-in account. Both
are identifiers, so writing the wrong one throws nothing, fails no constraint,
and simply credits a cashier's takings to whoever else holds that number.

The central account id is a ULID, not an integer, and `staff_members.user_id`
is sized for one. Declared numeric it worked on SQLite and nowhere else: MySQL
and PostgreSQL refuse the row, and a looser configuration coerces the ULID to
zero and points every staff row at one account that does not exist.
